WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.540
Download models from an approved source and verify the intended revision before spending

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:05.435
time loading them.

00:00:05.435 --> 00:00:08.580
A persistent cache or reusable disk can reduce repeated transfers,

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.435
but it continues to generate cost and must be protected.

00:00:11.435 --> 00:00:12.700
For disposable instances,

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.670
consider whether a clean automated download is safer and cheaper than retaining a large

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.540
cache between infrequent sessions.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.830
Quantization reduces memory demand and may allow a model to run on a smaller rental.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.900
Evaluate the quality and speed tradeoff with the actual task.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.420
Configure an inference server with explicit model, context, batch, and GPU settings,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.300
then expose it through an authenticated API.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.190
Keep the endpoint private while testing,

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.920
and apply request limits and timeouts before sharing it.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.580
Concurrency controls simultaneous sequences and increases cache and compute pressure.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.940
Batching can improve total throughput but may delay an individual request.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.990
Measure time to first output, prompt-processing speed, generation speed, queue time,

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.120
errors, and completed work per hour.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.780
Include network latency between the client and rental region.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.260
A fast benchmark inside the instance may not represent the user's end-to-end experience.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.140
Test real prompts, context lengths, documents, images, and failure cases.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:06.980
Watch VRAM, GPU utilization, CPU, RAM, disk, and network while the test runs.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:10.947
If the accelerator remains underused, identify whether tokenization, data transfer,

00:01:10.947 --> 00:01:15.215
queueing, or an unsupported backend is responsible before renting a larger device.

00:01:15.215 --> 00:01:18.720
The goal is the lowest-cost configuration that completes the workload reliably,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.460
not the largest GPU available.
